invariant: INV-16
file: keccak_hw.h
catches: test/hash-builds.sh
reason: keccak_hw.h stops renaming shake_absorb, so ML-KEM's two copies
  absorb their seeds on sha3.c's portable code while every other call of
  theirs runs on the instructions, and sha3_hw.c defines shake_absorb a
  second time. Every key and secret is still right, because both paths
  compute the same bytes. test/hash-builds.sh compiles the copies for
  arm64 under the pinned clang and requires each to call the _hw entry of
  every SHA-3 and SHAKE call it makes and none of sha3.c's.

--- old
#define shake_absorb shake_absorb_hw
--- new
